// How wide a single line a text input lets an edit make it (CappedLineEdit,
// WriteTagLineEdit). Slint's software renderer casts a text input's
// selection to 16-bit device pixels and panics past 32767 (DIFFERENCES.md,
// "Text inputs that take pasted lines"). The cap is in device pixels, as
// the limit is: 26000, leaving 6767 (26%) for a measurement that differs
// from what the input draws (the measuring text has the input's font family,
// size and style; a weight or fallback-font difference moves a line by a few
// percent) and for the selection's own rounding. At the default font that
// is about 4000 characters of a URL at a scale factor of 1, 2000 at 2, 1300
// at 3 (long_text_selection.rs).
export global TextCap {
    out property <float> device-pixels: 26000;
    out property <string> notice: "too long to enter here";
}
